itionsOrLines is co_positions' or co_lines' iterator."] [400 1 "// localsPlusNames is co_localsplusnames: the locals, the cells that are not parameters, the free variables."] [415 1 "// bcDecodeLines reads a location table (Objects/locations.md) into a location by code unit."] [472 1 "// replaced is the view of a code.replace(): co_code, co_consts, co_linetable and the others given (the machine still runs the IR)."] [489 4 "// co_lines and co_positions stop where the table does (a short table: no padding; queue 248)"] [511 1 "// atPC are the indices of the view's instructions IR instruction pc came from, in code order (queue 281)."] [524 1 "// branches are branchesiter_next's triples (queue 281): a FOR_ITER's (itself, the next instruction, past its target's"] [525 1 "// END_FOR and POP_ITER), a POP_JUMP_IF_*'s (itself, past its NOT_TAKEN, its target), an END_ASYNC_FOR's (its END_SEND,"] [526 1 "// past the END_SEND's NOT_TAKEN, the next instruction)."] [545 1 "// endSendOf is the offset of the END_SEND an END_ASYNC_FOR's oparg names (END_SEND_OFFSET past its target), -1 for none."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[172 18] [172 28] [179 18] [179 28] [181 29] [197 26] [197 33] [201 13] [201 25] [204 13] [204 20] [251 28] [251 36] [264 20] [305 18] [305 28] [308 18] [308 28] [339 22] [343 31] [344 14] [344 22] [345 18] [348 18] [360 22] [361 18] [379 13] [379 31] [465 7] [465 14] [537 29]]} (go/file "bytecode_asm.go" :imports [])

